WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.060
So no, this policy is not designed to-

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:03.060
I thought when I said it was a dumb question,

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:04.140
it meant no.

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:05.880
Well, I just want to be clear and precise.

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:08.020
I appreciate you trying to qualify my questions,

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:09.460
but nevertheless, I think it's a fair one

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:10.700
that a lot of people have.

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:13.180
My full answer is no, that is a lie

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:14.500
and it's a dumb question.

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:15.380
But you said something else,

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:16.860
speaking to the premise of one of your questions.

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:19.360
You said, well, aren't we provoking,

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:21.700
Illinois governor says we're provoking

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:23.500
actions that are unlawful.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:25.139
Why would the mere presence,

00:00:25.139 --> 00:00:26.520
just think about this for a second.

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:30.080
If I put federal law enforcement and national guard

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:31.780
into a nice sleepy Southern town.

